### Version 2.0.0 (unreleased)

- Refactored the SDK around one canonical C++ implementation and pybind11
  bindings under the existing `fourier_aurora_client` import.
- Added an explicit restartable singleton lifecycle with stopped-only
  configuration, selective endpoints, synchronous `stop()`, and queryable
  client and endpoint-match state.
- Added SDK-owned state, command, callback, result, and exception types while
  keeping the concrete FourierDDS facade publicly available.
- Added robot-independent C++ diagnostic clients and standalone GR3 C++ and
  Python workflow recipes.
- Added mock lifecycle/concurrency tests, real DDS loopback coverage,
  sanitizer profiles, installed-header and CMake-consumer checks, and a
  fresh-environment wheel loopback test.
- Unified native and Python version metadata at `2.0.0`, pinned package
  revisions, and added deterministic Debian and wheel artifact verification.
